Initialize Migration Environment: If you haven't done so already, you need to initialize the migration environment. This command will create a migrations directory in your project:
flask db init
Generate a Migration: After making changes to your models, you need to generate a migration script that captures those changes:
flask db migrate -m "Description of the migration"
Apply the Migration: Once you've generated the migration script, you need to apply it to your database:
flask db upgrade

Downgrade a Migration (Optional): If you need to rollback a migration, you can use the downgrade command:

flask db downgrade

celery -A website.make_celery beat --loglevel INFO
celery -A website.make_celery beat --loglevel DEBUG
celery -A website.make_celery worker --loglevel DEBUG

